Asha tells me Moti's rules before leaving.
She explains everything very carefully.
"Maya, Moti must be given food at exactly eight o'clock in the morning and evening," Asha says.
"Always feed him in his bowl only."
I nod in agreement.
"And in the park, he must always be kept on the leash," Asha continues.
"Taking off his leash in the park is strictly forbidden."
Moti sits on the floor and looks towards me.
"Can I give him my biscuits?" I ask.
"No Maya!"
"Giving him human food is strictly forbidden," Asha says immediately.
"He must only be given dog food."
"Do not give him anything else."
I listen carefully.
"Please do not worry at all, Asha," I say.
"I have understood all the rules."
"I will feed him at exactly eight o'clock."
"And I will always keep him on the leash."
Asha smiles and pets Moti.
"Thank you Maya, now I can leave peacefully," she says.
Asha goes outside and the door closes.
